      "title": "A death benefit and its interest are separate amounts",
      "narration": "Elena receives a qualifying two hundred thousand dollar death benefit plus three thousand dollars of separately stated interest. Assuming no exception to the ordinary death-benefit exclusion, the benefit is excluded from federal gross income and the interest is taxable. Choosing installments does not make all later interest disappear. Suppose the insurer holds a two hundred thousand dollar benefit for one hundred installments of twenty-four hundred dollars each. Under the stated fixed-installment calculation, two thousand dollars of each payment recovers the benefit, and four hundred dollars is interest. Life-contingent installments use additional calculations. Also check transfer-for-value and employer-owned coverage rules before assuming every death payment qualifies for the full exclusion.",
